From abf51ae6c2aed945d2ded74918d2272f850a0bea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:31:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] feat(installer): follow an XAPK's manifest.json and
 report what is not installed

An XAPK (APKPure's format) says in manifest.json which APKs form the
install (split_apks) and which expansion files go with it (expansions).
the other runtime ignored the file: it installed every .apk in the archive and
dropped the .obb entries without a word. An APKMirror .apkm that is
encrypted, not a ZIP, failed in the APK parser with a message that did
not say why.

- When manifest.json lists split_apks, those files are the install, each
  checked to be in the archive. Other archives without toc.pb keep
  taking every .apk entry.
- Expansion files (manifest.json's expansions and any .obb entry) are
  logged as not installed. Android keeps them in shared storage under
  Android/obb/<package>/, where Google Play or an XAPK installer puts
  them; a package install does not place them, and placing them here
  would need the other runtime's shared-storage ownership for that folder, which is
  left to a separate change rather than approximated.
- A .apkm that cannot be read as a ZIP is refused with
  INSTALL_FAILED_INVALID_APK naming the encrypted APKMirror format.
  the other runtime does not decrypt it.

PackageBundlesTest covers a v2 XAPK with split_apks, an unlisted APK, an
icon and an OBB; a v1 XAPK without split_apks; a manifest naming a
missing APK; a malformed manifest.json; and a ZIP whose entries are
marked encrypted.

